WHERE THE FULL THIRD-PARTY LICENCE TEXT IS

Inside the `.dmg`, under `Contents/Resources/licenses/`, assembled at build time. Every release also
carries two CycloneDX SBOMs — `sbom-main.json` and `sbom-renderer.json`, one per dependency tree —
on the main repository's release for the same tag. Two files because the application has two
dependency trees; one would describe half of it while reading as if it described all of it.

Naming the locations is deliberate. A NOTICE that says "licences are included" without saying where
cannot be checked, and this project has had that sentence be false before: an earlier version of it
claimed the build shipped licence text when the build shipped none.


NOT BUNDLED, AND DELIBERATELY SO

  CUDA and cuDNN are proprietary NVIDIA components and are never redistributed. A user who wants
  GPU acceleration installs them themselves.

  Model weights are not distributed with the application. They are downloaded by the user, and
  their licences are the model publishers' own.

  Research papers are not redistributed. arXiv's default licence grants distribution rights to
  arXiv, not to third parties. Papers are fetched by the user's own machine and never re-served.


ON SIGNING, BECAUSE IT IS A PROVENANCE CLAIM AND NOT A LICENCE ONE

The `.dmg` is ad-hoc signed — `codesign --sign -`, a signature with no identity — and NOT notarised.
The ad-hoc signature exists because Apple silicon refuses to execute an unsigned binary at all; it
is not an assertion of who built the file, and it must not be read as one. `SHA256SUMS.txt` is the
only provenance this distribution offers, and the README says how to check it.
